---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profileLinks } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Stefano Carlo Lambertenghi"
  description="About Stefano Carlo Lambertenghi, an autonomous-systems researcher working between software engineering, machine learning, and robotics."
>
  <section class="about-photo-section">
    <div class="about-portrait" data-reveal>
      <img
        class="about-portrait-photo"
        src="/images/me-and-fortuna.jpg"
        alt="Stefano Carlo Lambertenghi standing next to Fortuna"
        width="1400"
        height="1050"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <div class="about-portrait-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="about-portrait-label"><span>Munich, DE</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-hero page-hero-tight">
    <div class="page-hero-inner container-wide about-hero-compact">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About / researcher + engineer</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">About <em>me.</em></h1>
      </div>
      <p class="page-hero-copy">
        I’m Stefano, an autonomous-systems researcher working across software engineering,
        machine learning, and robotics.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="about-copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">The short version</p>
        <h2>Background.</h2>
        <p>
          At fortiss and the Technical University of Munich, I research how autonomous-driving
          tests transfer between simulated, mixed-reality, hardware-in-the-loop, and physical
          environments.
        </p>
        <p>
          That work is deliberately hands-on. It spans experimental design and peer-reviewed
          studies, but also ROS integration, sensors, vehicle interfaces, debugging, and the
          operational work needed to run a full-size research car safely and repeatedly.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before Munich, I studied artificial intelligence at USI in Lugano and worked at the
          Dalle Molle Institute for Artificial Intelligence (IDSIA) on embedded perception for
          autonomous nano-drones—fitting a relative-localization neural network onto a 40-gram
          quadrotor so it could track a peer drone in real time using a single onboard camera and
          under 100 mW of power (<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.01940" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">IEEE ICRA 2023</a>).
          The scale changed; the question did not: what has to be true for learned behavior to
          work outside the dataset?
        </p>
        <p>
          Mostly, I just like playing with hardware. Fortuna's recovery started as work and
          became a bit of a hobby; scanning it into a 3D model afterwards was an excuse to keep
          playing with it.
        </p>

        <dl class="about-details">
          <div><dt>Current</dt><dd>Researcher at fortiss · Doctoral researcher at TUM</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Focus</dt><dd>Testing and validation of autonomous systems</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Methods</dt><dd>Simulation, mixed reality, field experiments, empirical software engineering</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Platforms</dt><dd>Fortuna (full-size) and a small-scale Donkey Car research vehicle</dd></div>
        </dl>

        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a
            class="button button-dark js-email-link"
            href="#"
            data-email-user={profileLinks.emailUser}
            data-email-domain={profileLinks.emailDomain}
          >
            Email me
          </a>
          <a class="button button-dark" href={profileLinks.github} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>
          <a class="button button-dark" href="/cv/">View CV</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
